product}\\\\&\n a\\w b = \\frac{1}{2}(ab-ba)& \\text{definition of outer \
(wedge) product}\\\\&\n a\\w b={\\sum_{i<j}}\n[\\begin{matrix}\na_i&b_i\\\\\n\
a_j&b_j\\\\\n\\end{matrix}]\n\\e{i}\\w\\e{j} & \\text{in a coordinate form as \
sum of determinants\nmultiplied by elementary bivectors}\\\\&\n a\\w b=b a & \
\\text{if vectors are perpendicular}, \\quad a\\perp b\\\\&\n a\\w b=-b\\w a \
& \\text{outer product is antisymmetric}\\\\&\n a\\w b=0 & \\text{if vectors \
are parallel,}\\quad a\\| b\\\\&\n a\\w b={|a|}{|b|}\\sin\\theta\\,\\e{ab} \
&\\text{area of an oriented parallelepiped parallel to bivector \
}\\hat{\\e{}}_{ab}=\\frac{a\\w b}{|a\\w b|}.\n \\quad \\theta \\text{is the \
angle between  a and b  measured counterclockwise from a to b}\\\\&\n \
\\magnitude{a\\w b}={|a|}{|b|}\\mathrm{abs}(\\sin\\theta) \\qquad \
\\qquad&\\text{magnitude of outer product of vectors}\\\\&\n  \\pi \
r^2\\e{i}\\w\\e{j}=\\pi r^2\\e{ij}  &\\text{oriented area of a disk of radius \
}r\\\\\n\\end{aligned}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
